{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers","id":1092962,"title":"C20 Nockers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-15T14:46:49-07:00","id":1092962,"title":"C20 Nockers","content":"I checked carefully and nobody's brought this up, so I will.<br /> <br /> Nockers. What the cuck?<br /> <br /> Okay, I got that out. But seriously, this Kith feels like all of its teeth have been pulled. Sidhe Arts remained in the book, but Infusion is not there. I actually don't mind them no longer being the one special Kith that can manipulate Chimera to a degree no other can.... but the replacement is underwhelming. They don't feel like master crafters and inventors any longer. Let's break it down:<br /> <br /> New Frailty: Okay, I am down with this. It's left to ST imagination and judgement, and there is finally a system to that whole flaw thing. I can get behind that. But...<br /> <br /> New Birthright: Their replacement birthright is very... ill-formed. It's described as being temporary with no real mechanics and a very, very rough mechanic. They went from creating incredible devices and wonders to MacGyvering (not that I have anything against MacGyver) and repairwork (okay, they were always good at repairwork, but still). They're lacking in any sort of bonuses to show their crafty abilities, even the simple difficulty bonuses the old Kith had based on Court.<br /> <br /> Infusion: While the Sidhe Arts and many more obscure Arts stayed in, and many other Arts were re-worked into new places (Aphrodesia, Kryos), Infusion is nowhere to be seen. Though not exclusively Nocker, it was one of their big boons, and something of the sort would really go a long way toward helping them maintain their role as the mad scientists of the fae world.<br /> <br /> Listen, I know the old Nocker Birthright gave them a kind of unfair monopoly on crafting, but their new situation seems far too much of a swing in the opposite direction and leaves me uncertain how to possibly work with them now. Most of the other Kiths, the updates change them in various interesting ways, but they don't de-power them to the severe degree these do. I can't see a way right now for Nockers to keep being Nockers with their current skillset. Add in the new Frailty without anything to really balance it, and they're in a bad place here. No, it's not just about cool powers, but, well, those cool powers do to some degree define the Kiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:04:27-07:00","id":1092967,"title":"","content":"As a huge fan of Nockers, I like it. Never liked infusion even as a concept, and not having to be unseelie to do the cool crafting more than makes up for losing exclusivity. Plus I always liked McGuivering, and something similar has been a house rule in several games I played in before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:06:33-07:00","id":1092969,"title":"","content":"What do you think would make Nockers work in this new edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5211-firkraag","name":"Firkraag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5211_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:08:52-07:00","id":1092971,"title":"","content":"Soverign is no longer a Sidhe art either as far as everyone is explaining to me...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:11:27-07:00","id":1092974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1092971#post1092971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soverign is no longer a Sidhe art either as far as everyone is explaining to me...</div> </div> </div> </div>More importantly, neither is Naming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:18:15-07:00","id":1092975,"title":"","content":"I did not enjoy the MacGyvering either, it feels very out of place for a kith that is supposed to be perfectionist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:20:44-07:00","id":1092977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1092974#post1092974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More importantly, neither is Naming.</div> </div> </div> </div>or chronos for that matter","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:21:18-07:00","id":1092979,"title":"","content":"It's the hacker kith, not the perfectionist kith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:28:32-07:00","id":1092983,"title":"","content":"To quote C20, &quot; Nockers strive for perfection in everything they make...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:31:19-07:00","id":1092985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sinister Spider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1092983#post1092983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To quote C20, &amp;quot; Nockers strive for perfection in everything they make...&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, because they're hackers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:33:22-07:00","id":1092988,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CameraObscura83</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1092977#post1092977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> or chronos for that matter</div> </div> </div> </div>Naming was particularly horrible, as in 2nd ed by RAW naming had to be used after a year of the Changeling's existence or else they'll fall to Bedlam.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T16:45:51-07:00","id":1093017,"title":"","content":"Infusion is a horrible art. Only level 2 and 5 potentially provide something new and needed. Level 1 is innate as of c20, level 3 creates the whole category of needing special stuff to craft lightning guns and chimerical computers when.. it should be doable without and always requires fae 5, level 4 is &quot;you need this level to make a robot&quot; and can't say use anything but fae 5 again. Level 5 allows you to provide sapience to a chimerical object but much like level 2 redefines how realms work just to justify it not being fae 5. Its over all a complete mess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T18:04:44-07:00","id":1093044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093017#post1093017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infusion is a horrible art. Only level 2 and 5 potentially provide something new and needed. Level 1 is innate as of c20, level 3 creates the whole category of needing special stuff to craft lightning guns and chimerical computers when.. it should be doable without and always requires fae 5, level 4 is &amp;quot;you need this level to make a robot&amp;quot; and can't say use anything but fae 5 again. Level 5 allows you to provide sapience to a chimerical object but much like level 2 redefines how realms work just to justify it not being fae 5. Its over all a complete mess.</div> </div> </div> </div>But you have to admit the imagery of awesome robot golems roaming Goblin Town, built by the strange magical sciences and Arts that themselves are partially science, is a powerful and cool imagery.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T18:15:16-07:00","id":1093047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093044#post1093044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But you have to admit the imagery of awesome robot golems roaming Goblin Town, built by the strange magical sciences and Arts that themselves are partially science, is a powerful and cool imagery.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything is lost from that image by not having a specific Art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T18:32:30-07:00","id":1093051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093047#post1093047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think anything is lost from that image by not having a specific Art.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dunno, I liked that you had to invent an Art as part of the process to do what they did. It gave them a feeling of being an advanced society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T18:35:39-07:00","id":1093054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093051#post1093051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I dunno, I liked that you had to invent an Art as part of the process to do what they did. It gave them a feeling of being an advanced society.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not a special knowledge... like the book has Gemetria, Craft:Golum etc.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T18:36:39-07:00","id":1093055,"title":"","content":"Expert Knowledge perhaps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5533-cameraobscura83","name":"CameraObscura83","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T22:40:20-07:00","id":1093111,"title":"","content":"Infusion had its problems, but it gave them SOMETHING. They were mad scientists and artisans pushing the boundaries of what was possible. But their replacement Birthright is very... undefined. They gain no bonuses to Art or Crafts or any such thing. I honestly loved the golems, and the idea that level 5 was practically a sacred act. I love the guilds. But this new Nocker doesn't feel capable of forming guilds and crafting wonders. They certainly don't have the Birthrights to back that up. Sure, they can fix things. And they can make some vague temporary weird little gadget. But that's about it now. There's nothing other than flavor that speaks to them being master craftsmen, and nothing that prevents any other fae from doing the exact same thing it feels like. Heck, House Dougal does it BETTER now.<br /> <br /> I like the fact that their frailty MEANS something now. Part of the essence of the Nocker for me was always that perfectionist artist, who can never QUITE get it perfect, at least in their own mind. I don't know that this always needs to mean that their creations fail or explode, but a mechanic is nice. The problem is, there's a mechanic now for the flaw in their work, but nothing about how they actually MAKE those works. And no, the replacement doesn't cut it. It's very simplistic, states it's temporary, and frankly, as has been pointed out, does not have the feel of a specialist. It honestly feels a bit like it's just the other half of their other Birthright. Okay, so they're great at kludging things together. But where is the art? Where is the passion? Where are the masterworks, the airships, the hidden cities? The mechanics don't support that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3988,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","user":"Windthin","date":". 05-16-2017, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T23:05:35-07:00","id":1093119,"title":"","content":"For those who worked on this, by the by, please don't think I am trying to tear down what you've done. You put in SO much work. It's amazing. I and many others have waited so VERY long for this, to see Changeling brought into the 'modern' era as it were. I think there are areas that can be improved, but I LOVE so much of what has been done. I just... feel that Nockers don't work for me as Nockers right now. Clurichauns changed in their attitude somewhat, but I can still see them working. Piskeys are a bit different, and some others, but they still do what they do for the most part. I did not fail to notice how many popular powers were moved to new locations that often suited them better, how many were refined to be far more useful or far less, well, broken (I am looking at you Ensnare and your cannonball marbles). At present, though, I don't know how Nockers fit into this new updated world, and I am trying to figure that out by talking it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T23:06:43-07:00","id":1093122,"title":"","content":"Infusion wasn't the Nocker Birthright it was &quot;You can make Chimera&quot;(Except anything vaguely technological because SCIENCE BAD!). House Dougal was said to have people who had Infusion in the the Nocker book. Even in 2e the art was crap. Level 1 was litterally redundant for Nockers, for other kiths it gave them the abiltiy to make Chimera and still had shit inetraction with realms like actor.<br /> <br /> I do think giving them secret abilities that grant specific techniques may be the way to go, its not unprecidented in other gamelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T00:09:23-07:00","id":1093133,"title":"","content":"I didn't say Infusion was their Birthright. Also, the whole &quot;technology is bad&quot; thing is idiotic and many of the books contradict that. Lots of scientists have versatile, flexible, open minds. And a lot of the books show Nockers using their own bizarre form of science. I never got behind the idea that technology is inherently banal. Nockers for me were always the absolute proof that this was indeed not the case, that it could be just as creative and imaginative. Many of the old Arts had flaws. Ensnare was just plan broken while Veiled Eyes and Wind Runner suffered from severe duration issues. But the fundamental idea behind Infusion WAS a good one, an Art devoted to crafting, to creating. Look at how some former Arts live on: Kryos clearly is heavily invested in Winter now, and Aphrodesia is just one level of Summer, and I think that's fitting there. Holly Strike moved to an art of war, Heather Balm moved to Spring as Well of Life. I've done the comparison between old and new, and the changes are fascinating in many cases and places. I LOVE Pyretics' new ability to purify; it got a little bit TOO invested in setting things on fire, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Infusion was not exclusive to Nockers, I know. Some Boggans and members of House Dougal had it. But it was largely their thing, especially at higher levels; most non-Nocker Artisans only learned the first few levels, only needed to.<br /> <br /> The point, though, is that Nockers don't seem to have anything NOW that sets them apart as great artists and crafters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T05:52:34-07:00","id":1093194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093133#post1093133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say Infusion was their Birthright. Also, the whole &quot;technology is bad&quot; thing is idiotic and many of the books contradict that. Lots of scientists have versatile, flexible, open minds. And a lot of the books show Nockers using their own bizarre form of science. I never got behind the idea that technology is inherently banal. Nockers for me were always the absolute proof that this was indeed not the case, that it could be just as creative and imaginative. Many of the old Arts had flaws. Ensnare was just plan broken while Veiled Eyes and Wind Runner suffered from severe duration issues. But the fundamental idea behind Infusion WAS a good one, an Art devoted to crafting, to creating. Look at how some former Arts live on: Kryos clearly is heavily invested in Winter now, and Aphrodesia is just one level of Summer, and I think that's fitting there. Holly Strike moved to an art of war, Heather Balm moved to Spring as Well of Life. I've done the comparison between old and new, and the changes are fascinating in many cases and places. I LOVE Pyretics' new ability to purify; it got a little bit TOO invested in setting things on fire, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Infusion was not exclusive to Nockers, I know. Some Boggans and members of House Dougal had it. But it was largely their thing, especially at higher levels; most non-Nocker Artisans only learned the first few levels, only needed to.<br /> <br /> The point, though, is that Nockers don't seem to have anything NOW that sets them apart as great artists and crafters.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sums up my thoughts on them as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11321-sinister-spider","name":"Sinister Spider","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:49:19-07:00","id":1093216,"title":"","content":"I don't miss Infusion at all and any decent Storyteller is going to reward a Nocker's creativity and let them Build Cool Shit.The <b>Make It Work</b> Birthright is designed to let them magic Cool Shit on the fly and it doesn't replace their ability to Build Cool Shit that lasts longer. I do think there was a bit of a lost opportunity to utilize Professional Skill for forging chimera; Crafts seems a bit mundane when you're shaping dreams and magic. I think ditching exclusivity was a great design decision from an Arts perspective, both in terms of who can learn what Arts and which Realms can be used with them. <br /> <br /> The crafting system allows anyone to utilize it and be a crafter, which I think is great. Nockers get exclusive magic that no one else gets, the ability to build something on the fly from inappropriate materials that save the day or solve the problem. In terms of story, that is the coolest and I think will yield more memorable moments of satisfaction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:53:27-07:00","id":1093220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093133#post1093133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I didn't say Infusion was their Birthright. Also, the whole &amp;quot;technology is bad&amp;quot; thing is idiotic and many of the books contradict that. Lots of scientists have versatile, flexible, open minds. And a lot of the books show Nockers using their own bizarre form of science. I never got behind the idea that technology is inherently banal. Nockers for me were always the absolute proof that this was indeed not the case, that it could be just as creative and imaginative. Many of the old Arts had flaws. Ensnare was just plan broken while Veiled Eyes and Wind Runner suffered from severe duration issues. But the fundamental idea behind Infusion WAS a good one, an Art devoted to crafting, to creating. Look at how some former Arts live on: Kryos clearly is heavily invested in Winter now, and Aphrodesia is just one level of Summer, and I think that's fitting there. Holly Strike moved to an art of war, Heather Balm moved to Spring as Well of Life. I've done the comparison between old and new, and the changes are fascinating in many cases and places. I LOVE Pyretics' new ability to purify; it got a little bit TOO invested in setting things on fire, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Infusion was not exclusive to Nockers, I know. Some Boggans and members of House Dougal had it. But it was largely their thing, especially at higher levels; most non-Nocker Artisans only learned the first few levels, only needed to.<br /> <br /> The point, though, is that Nockers don't seem to have anything NOW that sets them apart as great artists and crafters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Man, am I ever the choir you are preaching to. This is why I hate the Technocracy being described as pure Banality.<br /> <br /> I've loved just about everything in this book, and I'm glad to see more stuff about Changelings and technology even if it's only a little, but I'd love to see maybe an entire book dedicated to Changelings finding the magic in the modern age.<br /> <br /> It sounds like they're pushing Nockers to be that Kith so I'd love to see more of that, maybe in a future book. But to your point about Infusion, I just wish they made it clearer how Nockers go about this because even the Chimera creation feels a bit vague and I just want to feel like Nockers have a clear advantage in this one thing.<br /> <br /> And while I generally dislike looking to the Houses for this sort of thing, as it means you MUST be a noble, at least we have the option to have Nockers of house Dougal","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:14:48-07:00","id":1093228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093220#post1093220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Man, am I ever the choir you are preaching to. This is why I hate the Technocracy being described as pure Banality.<br /> <br /> I've loved just about everything in this book, and I'm glad to see more stuff about Changelings and technology even if it's only a little, but I'd love to see maybe an entire book dedicated to Changelings finding the magic in the modern age.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> A friend of mine from the old Shadownessence forum had a project trying to do just that (am I allowed to say that here?) called the Book of Modern Dreams. He and I were thinking of getting that old project going again now actually.<br /> <br /> And I totally agree with you Windthin. Knockers feel like they have been overly nerfed. Even just a sidebar about how to apply Abilities and Resources to build things would be enough to balance the Knockers out I think. It would also give other kith the chance to build if they want to invest in the learning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T07:44:39-07:00","id":1093246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Urabyfirst</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093228#post1093228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> A friend of mine from the old Shadownessence forum had a project trying to do just that (am I allowed to say that here?) called the Book of Modern Dreams. He and I were thinking of getting that old project going again now actually.<br /> <br /> And I totally agree with you Windthin. Knockers feel like they have been overly nerfed. Even just a sidebar about how to apply Abilities and Resources to build things would be enough to balance the Knockers out I think. It would also give other kith the chance to build if they want to invest in the learning.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Shadownessence still around?<br /> <br /> If you're ever open to other input I have thoughts on this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T08:13:04-07:00","id":1093265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093054#post1093054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why not a special knowledge... like the book has Gemetria, Craft:Golum etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would actually prefer both. Like you have to draw on multiple specializations and even magics to make it happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T08:36:29-07:00","id":1093278,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I've had to put a lot of thought into this, I run Changeling on a site that has had it running for over a decade. For the longest time the site has been chockfull of House Rules because, well, there was no other way to run things. Old Changeling did a lot of things piecemeal. I have a whole write-up for fairy animals, and Nunnehi, and how to build freeholds, and so on and so forth. It was pretty much required, and now I am finding that a LOT of old house rules and fixes I can set aside with C20. You should see how much it's trimmed down my lists and such! Totally keeping the fairy animals, though, I based them on the horses and hounds from Kingdom of Willows.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, point is, technology is not bad. Disbelief is. Rigidity is. The Old Ways aren't any better, not when you adhere to them so strictly that you're blind to all else. ANYTHING can be banal if you spin it wrong. That guy obsessing over RBIs and collecting every single card can be a total Autumn Person... but a Clurichaun could be a collector of baseball cards with a great love of the game. A scientist can be a close-minded autocrat or a giddy wide-eyed wonderer. It's about mindset and method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T09:04:05-07:00","id":1093287,"title":"","content":"I was both elated and sad when I found out there was a section written for C20 that was cut out that included how the internet has pockets of the dreaming. It's that sort of thing I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> While I'm probably mentioning the technocracy too much for a changeling discussion, but only because i think they quickly express what I'm talking about, but I'd love to see it where the technocracy tends to have dreamers who dream of the future and attract Far but they view those same Far as a threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T10:47:51-07:00","id":1093328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093246#post1093246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Shadownessence still around?<br /> <br /> If you're ever open to other input I have thoughts on this <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately the Mists swallowed SnE a few months ago, leaving not a trace. A lot of great projects went with it. I was hoping they might reappear with the near release of C20.<br /> <br /> And I am more than happy to have input. I've started a thread in hopes that some of the old projects will surface.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","user":"Urabyfirst","date":". 05-16-2017, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3959-urabyfirst","name":"Urabyfirst","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:41:35-07:00","id":1093357,"title":"","content":"A player of mine pointed out that House Beaumayn has created an online MMORPG that has hidden Changeling sections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:23:01-07:00","id":1093372,"title":"","content":"I know we got off topic with regards to Nockers, and I totally didn't help, but am I the only one that feels the Krofted should almost be their own thing? Like, how there's Thallain and they are a darker reflection of Kithain. I'd love to see more groups like Manikins that take on concepts like digital entities of some sort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T12:51:53-07:00","id":1093386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mercurial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093265#post1093265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would actually prefer both. Like you have to draw on multiple specializations and even magics to make it happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's nothing &quot;Unmagical&quot; about the current crafting system. Giving Nockers basically &quot;Crafting Do&quot; while everyone else has to use Crafting Brawl seems about where I'd put it.. plus I don't have to figure out how how super Forging power works with Actor.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093287#post1093287\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was both elated and sad when I found out there was a section written for C20 that was cut out that included how the internet has pockets of the dreaming. It's that sort of thing I'd like to see.<br /> <br /> While I'm probably mentioning the technocracy too much for a changeling discussion, but only because i think they quickly express what I'm talking about, but I'd love to see it where the technocracy tends to have dreamers who dream of the future and attract Far but they view those same Far as a threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't understand the Technocracy as canon? You can run them however you want but just look at the Precepts of Daiman, the CODE of the Technocracy its not about discovery and knowledge its about Control and Stasis. The Syndicate primal Utility basically lets them Ravage people. That's what they do to dreams, drain them for power.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093372#post1093372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we got off topic with regards to Nockers, and I totally didn't help, but am I the only one that feels the Krofted should almost be their own thing? Like, how there's Thallain and they are a darker reflection of Kithain. I'd love to see more groups like Manikins that take on concepts like digital entities of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>Empire of Flickers gets a sentence or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 05-16-2017, 03:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:25:51-07:00","id":1093398,"title":"","content":"Arts in C20 were created with no kith-specific orientation.<br /> <br /> (In answer to something that came up on page 1.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":2494,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","user":"Rigistrade","date":". 05-16-2017, 04:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T14:19:29-07:00","id":1093415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093386#post1093386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't understand the Technocracy as canon? You can run them however you want but just look at the Precepts of Daiman, the CODE of the Technocracy its not about discovery and knowledge its about Control and Stasis. The Syndicate primal Utility basically lets them Ravage people. That's what they do to dreams, drain them for power.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no need to get nasty just because you don't agree. I never said there was no banality in the technocracy, but to say the entire technocracy is bad ignores those members that explore new reaches or make new discoveries which C20 itself points out as being a source of glamour.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093386#post1093386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Empire of Flickers gets a sentence or two.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true, though it's just one mention. I'm just hoping for more material in future books","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The only consistent wisdom is in knowing you know nothing&quot; ~ Socrates <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/PbrO9Kq.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1197-imthestein","name":"Imthestein","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1197_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T16:27:17-07:00","id":1093445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Imthestein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093415#post1093415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's no need to get nasty just because you don't agree. I never said there was no banality in the technocracy, but to say the entire technocracy is bad ignores those members that explore new reaches or make new discoveries which C20 itself points out as being a source of glamour.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't ascribe to the idea that banality is bad glamour is good. I do ascribe to the idea that the Technocracy KIND OF understands Banality and actively works to spread it because safety and control is their goal, with discovery being as a means to control. You know those bad scientists in media who scream &quot;This isnt' possible, this isn't scientific&quot; That's the Technocracy.. except they take it to the next step of shooting Unicorns. Theirs is a plan laid out for the future, it keeps getting bumped off course by all sorts of &quot;randomness&quot;<br /> <br /> This has nothing to do with science, you could just as readily have had the Order of Hermes pull the &quot;Our rules are the only rules kill anything outside it&quot; its just happened to people who liked guns over wands that did this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's true, though it's just one mention. I'm just hoping for more material in future books </div> </div> </div>I really hope a book of Gallain makes it in before 4/5e...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T16:35:30-07:00","id":1093448,"title":"","content":"I think equating science and the Technocracy is a bad idea in general. The entire premise of Mage makes Mages unable to employ the scientific method effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T08:26:44-07:00","id":1093664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093448#post1093448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think equating science and the Technocracy is a bad idea in general. The entire premise of Mage makes Mages unable to employ the scientific method effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>The premise of Mage isn't really compatible with a lot of things. Like,other games, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T08:31:42-07:00","id":1093665,"title":"","content":"I think it works just fine with Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:59:57-07:00","id":1093763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093398#post1093398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Arts in C20 were created with no kith-specific orientation.<br /> <br /> (In answer to something that came up on page 1.)</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of the Arts are noted as having originally been Sidhe-exclusive, though, and several are noted as being favored by certain Kiths also.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T17:24:38-07:00","id":1093910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093665#post1093665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it works just fine with Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, as at least one article of difference, Mage posits that all places are one place and only the perception changes, where as I'm pretty sure that Changeling has the Dreaming as some place that's fundamentally not of this world, differing perceptions or otherwise. It's akin to trying to squeeze the other games through a wire filter and getting a mess on yourself from it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T17:27:58-07:00","id":1093911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093910#post1093910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, as at least one article of difference, Mage posits that all places are one place and only the perception changes, where as I'm pretty sure that Changeling has the Dreaming as some place that's fundamentally not of this world, differing perceptions or otherwise. It's akin to trying to squeeze the other games through a wire filter and getting a mess on yourself from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a belief of some Traditions. It's not even universal across Mage, and it's not like the mechanics support that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T09:33:02-07:00","id":1094182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1093763#post1093763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A number of the Arts are noted as having originally been Sidhe-exclusive, though, and several are noted as being favored by certain Kiths also.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aye, in the past some Arts were tied to specific types of fae, but it was decided quite early on in the design process of C20 that the Arts making it into the book would be available to all Kiths. So while it's true that some favors certain Arts, none bars a certain Kith from using them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Krister M. Michl</b> <hr /><b>Freelance writer</b> <hr /><a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Krister_M._Michl\" target=\"_blank\">Entry on White Wolf Wikipedia</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2494-rigistrade","name":"Rigistrade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2494_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T02:33:47-07:00","id":1094469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rigistrade</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1094182#post1094182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aye, in the past some Arts were tied to specific types of fae, but it was decided quite early on in the design process of C20 that the Arts making it into the book would be available to all Kiths. So while it's true that some favors certain Arts, none bars a certain Kith from using them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose this does explain why we're NOT seeing special arts for Denizens, Thallain, and others, but I wonder if certain groups miss out by not having such access. I still do think an Art dedicated to crafting, something used by Boggans and Nockers and House Dougal and so on, would fit in nicely. But that only solves part of the problem that is the current lack of direction and skill Nockers have been given.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T05:40:42-07:00","id":1094495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Windthin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1094469#post1094469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose this does explain why we're NOT seeing special arts for Denizens, Thallain, and others, but I wonder if certain groups miss out by not having such access. I still do think an Art dedicated to crafting, something used by Boggans and Nockers and House Dougal and so on, would fit in nicely. But that only solves part of the problem that is the current lack of direction and skill Nockers have been given.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with an art used for Crafting is realms. While I feel Nockers could use a buff(their macguyver power is kind of confusing and doesn't work with long term stuff) I think that could be done via specialized abilities rather than trying to make an art that does this.<br /> <br /> Though maybe adding something liek Rituals/Rites might fill in gaps not just for Nockers but for other Fae tricks that don't need a full art.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T08:24:25-07:00","id":1094565,"title":"","content":"Infusion would work if, as with Metamorphosis, the Realm is determined by what you want to make. Prop to make a sword. Actor to make a golem. Nature to make a tree. Obviously, these are all chimerical items and Treasures.<br /> <br /> However, there is a general subsystem for Treasures now, which I think works, for the most part, to cover the ground Infusion covered. You could merge the missing elements of Infusion with some of those from Dreamcraft and Tale-Craft to make a new kind of chimera-specific shaping craft (Faecraft?).<br /> <br /> I mean, Pyretics was always pretty niche, and technically could have been subsumed into Primal, so there could still be a place for Infusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-19T21:27:46-07:00","id":1094773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1094565#post1094565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Infusion would work if, as with Metamorphosis, the Realm is determined by what you want to make. Prop to make a sword. Actor to make a golem. Nature to make a tree. Obviously, these are all chimerical items and Treasures.</div> </div> </div> </div>that's not how metamorphosis works at all. Actor doesn't let me change into people. it lets me target people. etc. More to the point why shouldn't all Treasures and Chimera be covered by their respective Fae realm?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, there is a general subsystem for Treasures now, which I think works, for the most part, to cover the ground Infusion covered. You could merge the missing elements of Infusion with some of those from Dreamcraft and Tale-Craft to make a new kind of chimera-specific shaping craft (Faecraft?). </div> </div> </div>Infusion has no missing elements. KB:Nocker basically created reasons why no one else can do things then an art for why Nockers can. The Core book started this trend with the whole &quot;no high tech in the dreaming&quot; all infusion added was the ability to get around this. I mean even its greatest power &quot;Make sapient mechanical chimera&quot; wasn't even necissary until CB:nocker. Nothing in the Nocker writeup says they couldn't make sapient Golems before that. It created a problem to be solved.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean, Pyretics was always pretty niche, and technically could have been subsumed into Primal, so there could still be a place for Infusion. </div> </div> </div>No, Infusion is just a bad art. Now there's room for giving Nockers(and eshu etc) abilities, Merits etc that give them greater capacity in their roles. These can even be supernatural abilities like Kenning. There even might be room for more limited powers for the Fae that aren't arts based. But infusion was a bad art.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T01:50:58-07:00","id":1094808,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I was thinking of Oneiromancy. Still not used to the new rules. With Oneiromancy, you create items in dreams using Realms (so Prop to make new items or bring them into the dream). That way, it works beyond just Fae 5.<br /> <br /> Infusion could be covered by a Knowledge too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-20T15:28:32-07:00","id":1094957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1092962-c20-nockers?p=1094808#post1094808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, I was thinking of Oneiromancy. Still not used to the new rules. With Oneiromancy, you create items in dreams using Realms (so Prop to make new items or bring them into the dream). That way, it works beyond just Fae 5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Level 2 Oneromancy still doesn't end up with some oddly redundant bits, because what you create is also a Trigger for the person in the real world there's a difference between making a Dream chimera and a dream animal, object etc.<br /> <br /> Level 5 which allows the manifestation of a dream concept as a chimera is limited to the dreams of the target.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have quite the level of redundancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Infusion could be covered by a Knowledge too. </div> </div> </div><br /> There are plenty of abilties spread through the games that are more powerful than just adding dice to a certain roll. Granting capabilities beyond standard mortal powers. Having something like this to cover Infusion in Talecraft is my suggestion rather than trying to remake them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-09T13:48:03-07:00","id":1138987,"title":"","content":"I also didnt liked the exchanged of the old Birthright for the new one, because it makes the Nockers far less the Chimerical Inventors and Innovators, as not only the Boggans are more reliable (can't botch Craft) and faster (1/3 of the time) but also dont have annoying Imperfections and a chance of a explosive results (as they do not have the Nocker frailty). There is no point in making a builder or a inventor as a Nocker instead of a Boggan, as there is no limitation of how inventive can a Boggan be.<br /> <br /> Not saying the old birthright was perfect, if anything it was a little too extreme, making Nockers the only Kith that could do those things, but I think the exchange took too much from the Kith, as the new birthright of making stuff on the run seems... unworthy. Is cool, no doubt about it, MacGyver is always cool, but is definitely unpair with what should be the dreams of builders and inventors.<br /> <br /> And thinking about it I got an idea. The C20 on the part about Treasure, they say treasures can gain an smaller special feature when they became stuff of legends, like extra damage against undead for a sword known to kill Vampires. But it takes time, effort and a bunch of adventures. My suggestions in giving the Nocker the ability to make the most epic itens they create getting out of the forge with it.<br /> <br /> Of course it isnt everything. Only the most hard (15+ success on the Craft roll) and Glamour infused (an expenditure of a Glamour point per day of work) pieces of work, made with the best materials (only the best chimerical ingredients) and the greatest purposes (need to have a inherent purpose and owner, cant be just to be put to sale) would deserve such magnificent ability.<br /> <br /> The power would be related to the purpose and materials. 3 examples:<br /> <br /> - A sword made of Moon Silver, forged to the the most noble knight of house of Gwydion with the purpose to free the city of the despicable Thallains that rampage the streets would come with the power to shine with their proximity of a Thallain and to detect through their disguises and illusions.<br /> <br /> - A battering Ram, made with logs from the Forgotten Forest and with the skull of a Chimerical Dire Goat on the front, made so that the Commoner rebellion can finally brake through the Sidhe castle and install a democracy over the tyranny, would be even more powerful against oppression symbols of the noblemen (like castles, walls, etc.) and would render those, after broke, unfixable.<br /> <br /> - A Jade Collar, made with Jade brought by the Hsien direct from a sacred Dragon's Nest on Tibet, made to be given to the most beautiful princess from a Satyr lover as a prove that he loves her, and only her, would, over the moon light, show to her where he is and grow dark does he ever be unfaithful or stop loving her.<br /> <br /> A Nocker doesnt make the objects planning those powers, they come naturally and more or less unexpectedly (so they are decided by the ST), but the Nocker can have some general idea in mind (the player can give a general idea of what he wants, but the ST is not, by any means, bound to it). Also, not everything the Nocker tries to put this effect on will work, specially if the Nocker is trying to over use this effect to make a battalion of Thallain hunters or an unbeatable army. The Nocker cant use this effect to make something that &quot;will not be use until the right time&quot; or &quot;the sole purpose is to never be found&quot;.<br /> <br /> The Nockers would also keep the Improvising Birthright, cause it is also cool and very useful, and I dont think keeping both is OP. (But I might be convince otherwise).<br /> <br /> What do you guys think?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12934-manbat","name":"Manbat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12934_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T18:06:51-07:00","id":1142364,"title":"","content":"The one thing that makes Nockers likely to make these things and Boggans not is... setting. Boggans prefer simple crafts, Nockers like their mad science. But the point remains that, mechanically, Boggans do it better. Anyhow, here is my re-jiggering of Infusion: <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"http://wodcityofangels.com/images/Changeling/Infusion.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> This is the fundamental Art of Nocker craft, and most Nockers are conversant with its principles. At its lowest levels, Infusion strengthens and alters chimerical materials, making them easier for changelings to manipulate and work with. At its highest levels, this Art is an act of creation in the truest sense.<br /> <br /> Infusion is based in part on the premise that there are three basic types of chimera: Incidental, Dreamed, and Forged. Incidental chimera are flimsy and difficult to work with in their native forms, but are also by far the most common form of chimera. They are fleeting and ephemeral, dreamed into existence for a few seconds before evaporating like smoke. This is also the most common kind of chimera found in the physical world, spun of daydreams and idle thoughts. Mortals cannot see them, and they quickly succumb to the ravages of Banality, especially if they are removed from the area where they came into being.<br /> <br /> Dreamed chimera are somewhat hardier, able to survive indefinitely after the reverie that created them ends. Dreamed chimera spring from the minds of changelings and mortals, and are the most common type of chimera found in the Dreaming. They still can wither swiftly in the face of Banality, though.<br /> <br /> A big factor in whether or not they can survive is what inspired them and where they are. More malleable, half-formed objects are also more fragile, while something like the chimerical reflection of Notre Dame Cathedral is a towering, fully-formed wonder that stands strong and firm. The more notable the inspiration for a chimera is, the stronger its reflection. A pancake house may have a reflection in the Dreaming, but it is crude and in a state of flux, shifting with every new customer that comes through the doors. The pancake house's reflection is largely Incidental, while Notre Dame's is definitely Dreamed.<br /> <br /> Virtually all animate chimera are fully formed and realized, but they are also fewer in number, the population to fill the scenery. Most aren't sentient, but many can pass for it. Often the best, strongest, and most difficult-to-obtain components for chimerical item crafting come from animate chimera; a shield crafted of inanimate emeralds might have its binding emblem made of leather taken from a conquered dragon chimera.<br /> <br /> Forged chimera are those crafted by Nockers and other talented artisans. They fall somewhere between the categories of chimera into their own classification. At one time, anybody could easily pull wonders from thin air, crafting draw dreamstuff with the force of their own will, but with the arrival of the Sundering and Shattering, those days are long past, at least in the Autumn World. Dream manipulation is not what it once was; while they can still create simple things like their voile at whim, creating and banishing them, and skilled Oneiromancers able to pluck items from Dreams and make them manifest temporarily are in demand, there is something to be said for the permanency of items crafted by skilled artisans.<br /> <br /> Forged chimera are crafted out of materials gathered from Dreams and the Dreaming and put together in laboratories, workshops, and garages. These include many treasures and more potent chimerical items as well as actual animate creations like clockwork and robotic servants, steeds, and pets; in recent years, many of these show a marked steampunk aesthetic due to the growing popularity of this genre.<br /> <br /> Most who make animate chimera settle for a semblance of life; true sentience is quite difficult to create. On truly rare occasions, though, it does spontaneously ignite, and these events are becoming gradually more common due to march of technology and human fears and hopes of true artificial intelligence.<br /> <br /> While forged chimera can be created without the Art of Infusion, its use makes the task easier. It was developed over the long centuries of the Interregnum, as a method of coping with the loss of Glamour and magic. It was originally the creation of Nockers, crafted from a variety of scientific and pseudo-scientific pursuits in alchemy, gematria, astrology, and similar pursuits. While the exact date for when it became a fully-fledged Art is impossible now to determine, some believe that it saw its culmination during the early Renaissance period. For a long time the Nocker guilds held tight rein on this art, with few from other Kiths able to ever learn more than the basics, if that. However, as the Age of Exploration opened up the world and new views of liberation and freedom spread, so too did knowledge. Sometimes it was rogue Nockers sharing their secrets, sometimes other Kiths working out the principles themselves or getting a hold of Nocker texts. The Bes Din, the Nocker governing council, tries to clamp down on this, but eventually had to accept that this was impossible, so chose instead to act as the primary source for Infusion; to this day, most who learn the Art register with the Bes Din.<br /> <br /> While Nockers see this Art as something of a science, many others see it more as an Art. There are lines crossed, as there are truly in many fields, for a blacksmith must have both artistic style and technical skill.<br /> <br /> Because it IS an Art of the Autumn World, crafted after the Shattering, newly-arrived Arcadian Kithain won't ever have any knowledge of it. Some Arcadians look down their noses at this Art, but others, particularly members of House Dougal, have been fascinated by its development, and House Dougal is without a doubt one of its strongest supporters now.<br /> <br /> For obvious reasons the most frequently-used Realm with this Art is Prop. However, many of the lower levels can be used in other creative ways to bolster and strengthen the chimerical world.<br /> <br /> <b>Unleashing Infusion</b><br /> Infusion at its heart is about creation. Unleashing it is rare, but can occur; a desperate attempt, for instance, to strengthen and save a fading chimerical companion or beloved heirloom about to be unraveled by Banality. Unleashings are accompanied by great bursts of power and energy, often in the form of electricity, light, and heat. Example commands might be &quot;save my friend&quot; or &quot;bolster my shield.&quot;<br /> <br /> <b>Infusion Bunks</b><br /> Infusion bunks are some of the easiest and most obvious to imagine; they involve crafting. Hammering, smelting, sewing, tinkering. Even the most hastily-drawn bunk usually involves the tools and trappings of an artisan; a ringing hammer, a few quick stitches of a needle through one's own flesh.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wodcityofangels.com/images/Changeling/InfusionDots.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Harden</b></span><br /> This cantrip allows a changeling to &quot;harden&quot; Incidental chimera into a form that can be forged. The target effectively goes from Incidental to Dreamed. Its fate from there depends on what happens next. Left exposed to Banality, it could still soon disappear. Harvested or moved to a more receptive environment, though, the object could survive and stabilize, and perhaps even gain more detail and cohesion.<br /> <br /> Though typically used in Inanimate chimera, this CAN be used on the Animate. It is not commonly done, as the results can be unpredictable, as a nebulous sprite suddenly becomes a more coherent creature shaped by whatever whimsy might be in the air.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: This cantrip costs at least one point of Glamour always; that Glamour is required to bolster the chimera being affected. The Realm used is determined by the nature of the chimera affected; use the appropriate realm for the non-chimerical counterpart. This means anything inanimate will be Nature or Prop, anything animate will be Nature or Actor; a building or park would be Scene. Fae may be used as a secondary realm but never the primary realm for this cantrip.<br /> <br /> An Incidental chimera that has had this cantrip successful cast upon it can be forged as if it were a Dreamed chimera.<br /> <br /> The number of successes determines the duration of the cantrip. For purposes of crafting, this often means you need at least two successes for it to be of much use, but for some other purposes one success could do, like giving that enchanted bully's fear of his old neighbor's pit bull sudden definite form.<br /> <br /> 1 success - One hour<br /> 2 successes - One day<br /> 3 successes - One week<br /> 4 successes - One month<br /> 5 successes - Permanent<br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Chimerical<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://wodcityofangels.com/images/Changeling/InfusionDots.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><img src=\"http://wodcityofangels.com/images/Changeling/InfusionDots.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Toughen</b></span><br /> This allows a changeling to toughen any chimerical material (even a changeling's fae mien), making it more resistant to damage and Banality.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: As with Harden above, the nature of the chimerical object to be affected determines the Realm needed for casting. Using this on changelings requires Fae. Also, at least one Glamour must be spent.<br /> <br /> Any chimerical substance affected by this cantrip gains an additional Health Level for every two successes earned by the casting of the cantrip. In addition, all rolls for resisting Banality are reduced by one for every two successes gained.<br /> <br /> Multiple castings of this cantrip do not have cumulative effects. When used on chimera, the effects are permanent. When used on a changeling, they only last for the scene, and extra health levels gained disappear when damage is taken.<br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Chimerical<br /> <br /> <b>OOO </b><span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>FUBAR Generation</b></span><br /> While electricity is not unknown in the chimerical world, it usually either takes the form of lightning or some kind of strange Nocker machine that arcs to anything nearby \u2014 most things that ought to use electrical power to operate run instead on steam, water, wind, or pure Glamour. Even most nocker-tech runs on steam; having been around for centuries, steam is the easiest power source to create in the Dreaming, dating back to Roman times. The fae, and particularly Nockers, were far ahead of humanity in its harnessing, and Changeling steam-power is vastly more potent.<br /> <br /> This Cantrip is the primary method for gathering the power source for any sort of chimerical device that uses electricity or magnetism. Nockers and others have found that much advanced science works poorly in the Dreaming, things like chemical reactions. Even things like explosions and combustion don't quite work the same, which is why chimerical firearms are so very difficult and expensive to craft.<br /> <br /> At the heart of harnessing electricty in the Dreaming is the FUBAR, also known as Will-o-the-Wisps, Ignis Fatuus, Fiar's Lanterns, Jack-o-Lanterns, Hinkypunks, Hobby Lanterns, Brujahs, Luces del Dinero, Luces del Tesoro, Fi Follet, Feu-Follet, and dozens more names depending on where you look. Seriously, check out the wiki article, there's all kinds of info on the different terms for these.<br /> <br /> What they are for the Changelings are bobbing little energy fields, sources of pure Glamour that break numerous laws of physics. For instance, unlike magnets that must have two poles, some FUBARs have only one, positive <i>or</i> negative. Many also seem to have a mind of their own, and some have even been known to get temperamental or 'go bad.'<br /> <br /> Their real-world Wyrd component is well-known by scientists and stories, associated most often with swamps and lowlands.<br /> <br /> This cantrip allows for a changeling to spontaneously <i>create</i> FUBARs and bend them to his well. It is not actually known if this cantrip creates FUBARs or simply summons them, but either way this cantrip allows for the easy collecting of them, much easier surely than going out and trying to capture wild ones.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: While Fae 5 is best for fully manipulating FUBARs, Fae 3 is all that is required to summon one. Anything less will require an Unleashing, and I don't need to tell you the dangers of using an Unleashing to summon a powerful source of Glamour.<br /> <br /> This cantrip also only summons the FUBAR; actually containing it is another matter. Naturally, most will have some sort of containment set up ahead of time. These can be surprisingly simple; a metal hoop, a crystal sphere, a wire globe. A changeling can trap a generated FUBAR with an Intelligence + Science or Gremayre roll, with an appropriate specialty in Gematria (the most common Nocker specialty) or a similar esoteric field of study. The number of successes determines the number of Glamour points the FUBAR has.<br /> <br /> A point of Glamour must be spent to use this cantrip; whether it acts as the seed for the FUBAR or a lure is again a subject of debate.<br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Chimerical<br /> <br /> OOOO <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Animantis</b></span><br /> Golems are the automated servitors of Nockers, and most serve and accompany their creators willingly. Like all chimera, golems may range widely in power, size, and appearance. Like all chimera, they may range widely in power, size, and appearance. The only constraints on a golem's features or capabilities are an artist's talents, materials, and imagination. Most golems have a mechanical appearance, though the use of certain cantrips like Smoke and Mirror (Legerdemain 5) can help to project a more natural appearance. While this method is not the only one to make chimerical companions, it is one of the most potent and stable methods, in part due to the use of a FUBAR and well-established techniques.<br /> <br /> Golems of old often looked like the &quot;traditional&quot; clay humanoids, suits of armor, or intricate wind-up, clockwork, and mechanical animals. As technology has risen, so has the arrival of '50s science-fiction movie and pulp-fiction robots, steampunk automatons, and anime-inspired androids. Golems are often crafted as pets and beats of burden also, taking on animal forms both familiar and fantastic.<br /> <br /> <b>System</b>: You must have at least Fae 4 to be able to use this power.<br /> <br /> Golem creation is an arduous process, even by this method. To create a golem there are four principle steps:<br /> <br /> 1) Gathering the materials. This includes anything necessary to make the golem itself, plus possible machinery to power it up and the FUBAR.<br /> <br /> 2 &amp; 3) The golem's creation. This involves two sets of extended rolls. The first is Intelligence + Science or Gremayre with an appropriate specialization like Gematria, the second is Intelligent + Crafts. The base difficulty is 4 plus the level of the golem, with the chart below laying out the number of successes required and the number of points you get to build with. Each roll equals two full days of work (at least eight hours a day); golem creation is a lengthy process. Use the basic Crafting rules in C20 otherwise. You can shoot for more successes if you want to add greater aesthetic detail to your golem.<br /> <br /> Golem creation works the same way as Chimerical Companion creation, though for some particularly potent Redes you may need special materials. Treat powers like Legedermain 5 to give the golem a more natural appearance as you would Treasure creation. All golems created via this method are non-sentient initially, meaning you can not buy Willpower with these points. They can be programmed to seem quite life-like, especially when components from animate chimera are used, but ultimately they are not sentient.<br /> <br /> A non-sentient golem's Intelligence and Wits may not exceed its level; Perception has no such limit. Therefore, a level 1 golem could have a maximum of 1 dot each in Intelligence and Wits. Skills and Knowledges are the best way to augment a non-sentient golem's skill set.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you must obtain a FUBAR of at least the level you are trying to create; every dot of Glamour the FUBAR possesses over the level you're shooting for translates as one free starting dot of Glamour for the creation, up to a level equal to the golem's level +1. Yes, this does mean it's easier to power up lesser creations. The process of successful animating a golem uses up the FUBAR, though it can affect the transfer of sentience if this is part of the process (See Gilgul below).<br /> <br /> Level 1: A conversation piece, simple pet, or minor servant. Typically capable of simple functions and commands or low level mimicked behavior. 20 to 25 points, minimum 10 successes for each stage to reach minimum level, plus 1 success on the Crafting roll only for each point up to maximum (so 5 extra successes for a 25 point golem).<br /> <br /> Level 2: A minor golem, semi-intelligent and able to communicate and be of assistance. Commands must still be fairly simple, mimicked behavior can often seem more convincing. 26 to 30 points, minimum 15 successes for each stage, plus 1 success on the Crafting roll only for each point up to maximum.<br /> <br /> Level 3: A useful golem, often capable of clear speech and an ability to carry out more in-depth instructions and commands or pass as sophisticated. 35 to 40 points, minimum 20 successes for each stage, plus 1 success on the Crafting roll only for each point up to maximum.<br /> <br /> Level 4: A golem of significant power, able to understand and carry out complex commands and duties and even look self-aware. 45 to 50 points, minimum 25 successes for each stage, plus 1 success on the Crafting roll only for each point up to maximum.<br /> <br /> Level 5: A very powerful golem, just this side of truly sentient often, able to follow a wide array of plans and functions. 65 to 70 points, minimum 30 successes for each stage, plus 1 success on the Crafting roll only for each point up to maximum.<br /> <br /> Yes, this means that it can take over four months to craft a very powerful golem, not including the gathering of materials. Given what they are capable of, you can see why there is demand, particularly because most golems are loyal servants, forged and crafted for the individual they are intended for and thus less flighty than a dreamed-up beast or some legendary chimera that is tracked down and tamed.<br /> <br /> 4) Once the golem's body is built, the changeling must hook it up to a FUBAR-powered generator. That is when this Cantrip is cast, initiating the process to effectively power it up. A botched cantrip roll means the animation process caused physical damage to the golen and the creator must repair it before making another attempt. A point of Glamour must be spent to initiate the process, after which the FUBAR takes over.<br /> <br /> No matter how life-like it may seem, any golem created through this process is only going through the motions. To imbue actual life into the golem requires the next level of this Art, and thus a fifth step. Some rare golems DO come into awareness on their own; this is an entirely random affair that can not be readily predicted.<br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Chimerical<br /> <br /> OOOOO <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><b>Gilgul</b></span><br /> Gilgul is the Hebrew term for &quot;transmigration of souls,&quot; &quot;reincarnation,&quot; or &quot;metamorphosis.&quot; For Nockers, it is the ultimate act of creation, for it is the process by which sentient life is created. Bestowing the breath of life involves advanced levels of study and skill; the beliefs on this have evolved over time. Many modern Nockers, for instance, talk in terms of monads, similar to quarks, though obviously this is a relatively recent development and this ability goes back much farther.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the process involves a great deal of time and equipment. This cantrip is most frequently used to bring golems fully to lfie as thinking beings, but can also be used to grant any non-sentient chimera sentience.<br /> <br /> Nockers take this level of their Art extremely seriously. After several incidents involving rogue Golems and rogue golem creators, they easily convinced the Concordia Parliament of Dreams to pass laws requiring anybody making use of the two highest levels of Infusion to be licensed and registered with the Grand Bes Din. They've also managed this feat in many other Kithain nations. Separate permits are required to levels 4 and 5, and the Grand Bes Din is on the watch for illegal golem creators. They reserve their most severe censure for those who would misuse Gilgul, though, for to them it is a truly sacred act. There are many Kithain who learn only Animantis and never progress to the final level for a variety of reasons, from being turned down to creating golems only for purposes where sentience might be seen as a flaw and not a boon.<br /> <br /> System: When granting sentience to a golem, the Realm Fae 5 (Dweomer of Glamour) must always be used. Obviously, using Unleashing to achieve this would be an act of true and utter madness. When using this cantrip on other chimera, the nature of the chimera determines the Realm used, though Fae 5 can be used as a secondary Realm.<br /> <br /> The Changeling must design a device to transfer an imprint of another sentient being's brain patterns onto his creation. This tends to involve rare materials; for example, one modern Nocker used a rod of true silver and a delta-wave helmet to collect strange monads for this purpose. Whatever the case, the device must be built and a mind found for the imprint. Many Nockers choose to use their own brains, naturally, but this does not have to be the case. Some have experimented with having two or more minds involved in the process, in the hopes of creating a unique composite. While this can indeed create a more unique individual, it is also more difficult to guarantee what personality traits might transfer to the awakened creation.<br /> <br /> The device for the transfer is considered a work of Complex crafting under C20 creation rules; fortunately, once one is possessed, it can be re-used provided it was not destroyed in some lab mishap, so some might instead seek out the equipment of a previously successful craftsman.<br /> <br /> No matter what, a FUBAR is required to power the transfer. For golems, this is usually the same FUBAR that gave them life; if this is the case, add 1 to the golem's base Willpower for every two dots of Glamour left in the FUBAR after the amount that goes into free Glamour points. Round down.<br /> <br /> <i>Example:</i> A Nocker wants to power up a Level 2 golem using a Glamour 6 FUBAR. 3 of those points get transferred as an automatic base Glamour rating. 3 remain, raising the starting of the Willpower of the golem by 1 when Gilgul is activated.<br /> <br /> For already active golems or chimera, subtract the creatures level +1 from the Glamour total of the FUBAR and then apply it the same way.<br /> <br /> <i>Example:</i> A kindly Boggan wants to grant sentience to his Pooka friend's stuffed skunk friend. The chimera is only level 2, and the FUBAR holds a whopping 9 Glamour, so that leaves 6 after the initial drain, or a +3 to its base Willpower. That is one determined little skunk.<br /> <br /> Sentient golems and awakened chimera can range from dimwitted to remarkably intelligent. Make use of the chimera's natural Mental Attributes as a base line. When sentience is granted, these go from being rote behaviors and programmed knowledge to a full measure of awareness. The degree to which this awareness goes is determined by a single Intelligence + Science or Gremayre roll, with the appropriate specialty, at difficulty 7, made after the Cantrip roll. The Cantrip roll is all or nothing; if it succeeds, you have a sentient chimera. The creature is friendly and loyal to its creator and/or imprint source and learns fundamental skills quickly. Over time, it may develop its own personality traits, or some may carry through from the imprint source.<br /> <br /> If it fails, you'll have to boot everything back up and try again.<br /> <br /> And if one or both rolls botch, the golem gains sentience but the Gilgul goes horribly awry; the golem or chimera is mentally unstable and antisocial (though this may not be immediately apparent). The creator of a rebellious or out-of-control golem or chimera may have to destroy her child to prevent a bloody rampage, something every Nocker fears.<br /> <br /> No successes: The golem or chimera actually LOSES any degree of intelligent it previously had and is a blithering idiot. It may actually be less useful than it was before, if it was animated previously. The chimera can't even follow simple instructions, but is still alive and aware and loves its master like a half-witted dog would. Creating a fool is one of the risks of creating life, and puts the creator in a moral dilemma of caring for his child or extinguishing its life and hoping the Bes Din NEVER gets word of it. The golem has a Willpower rating equal to the donor's Willpower -1, so you may wind up with a half-witted but determined pet.<br /> <br /> 1 Success: The golem or chimera has a child-like attitude and mentality, and always will. It may exhibit one or two broad traits either from the donating mind or the donator's desires and dreams. The chimera or golem has a base Willpower of 1 and you have 2 dots you can add to Willpower or Mental or Social Attributes.<br /> <br /> 2 Successes: The golem or chimera likely has a child-like attitude and mentality which may slowly develop to something more mature, though rarely beyond what one might expect of a teenager. It may exhibit one or two broad traits either from the donating mind or the donator's desires and dreams. The chimera or golem has a base Willpower of 2 and you have 2 dots you can add to Willpower or Mental or Social Attributes.<br /> <br /> 3 Successes: The golem or chimera often begins with a child-like sense of wonder that will evolve over time depending on how it is treated, and can fully 'mature.' The chimera is likely to exhibit several major traits either from the donating mind or the donator's desires and dreams and develop more of a personality over time. The chimera or golem has a base Willpower of 3 and you have 3 dots you can add to Willpower or Mental or Social Attributes.<br /> <br /> 4 Successes: The golem or chimera may begin with a child-like sense of wonder that will evolve over time depending on how it is treated, and can fully 'mature,' or may begin with a more advanced and well-rounded psyche. The chimera is likely to exhibit a good number of major traits and quirks either from the donating mind or the donator's desires and dreams and develop more of a personality over time. The chimera or golem has a base Willpower of 4 and you have 4 dots you can add to Willpower or Mental or Social Attributes.<br /> <br /> 5 Successes: The golem or chimera may begin with a child-like sense of wonder that will evolve over time depending on how it is treated, and can fully 'mature,' or may begin with a more advanced and well-rounded psyche. The chimera is likely to exhibit a good number of major traits and quirks either from the donating mind or the donator's desires and dreams and develop more of a personality over time. The chimera or golem has a base Willpower of 5 and you have 5 dots you can add to Willpower or Mental or Social Attributes.<br /> <br /> Every two successes beyond 5 adds another dot you can add to Willpower or Mental or Social Attributes; base Willpower does not rise. Such golems or chimera often exhibit uncanny degrees of wisdom and personality.<br /> <br /> A sentient golem has no level cap for Mental Attributes like a non-sentient one does, so you could wind up with a highly intelligent level 1 golem.<br /> <br /> <b>Type</b>: Chimerical<br /> <br /> PS: Had to remove some of the gear dots, as apparently I am limited to 4. The title looks better on a dark background.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T19:28:08-07:00","id":1142378,"title":"","content":"It still doesn't look like an art like the other arts. It looks like a Square peg being slammed into a round hole. I think secret techniques of the nockers is better covered by abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-20T21:48:54-07:00","id":1142413,"title":"","content":"Except they're not covered. At all. And if you look there are other Arts that are unlike others, like Contract, which has its own very unique workings, or Chronos.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3988-windthin","name":"Windthin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3988_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}